    "raw": "---\ntitle: 'Autonomous Satellite Tracking System'\npublishedAt: '2025-05-15'\ndateRange: 'Aug 2024 - May 2025'\nsummary: 'Built an automated computer vision system that tracks Low Earth Orbit satellites at 120 FPS using high-speed cameras, orbital physics models, and motorized mounts.'\ntechStack: 'Python, C++, C, C#, TypeScript, JavaScript, OpenCV, PyTorch, YOLO, ML.NET, SGP4/TLE, React, ASP.NET MVC, .NET Core, Embedded Linux, Serial Protocols, SQL, Bash'\n---\n\n## The Problem\n\nLow Earth Orbit satellites travel at about 17,000 miles per hour. From the ground, an overhead pass lasts only two to three minutes through a telescope lens.\n\nTo a camera sensor, a satellite looks like a tiny faint speck moving fast against a background of bright stars. Trying to aim and track that by hand is nearly impossible.\n\nAt Lake Superior State University (Aug 2024 - May 2025), I wrote software to calculate when satellites pass overhead, detect them in live camera video, and steer motorized telescope mounts to track them automatically.\n\n---\n\n## What I Built\n\n* **120 FPS vision pipeline**: Wrote C++ and OpenCV code to process video feeds at 120 frames per second to keep up with fast-moving targets.\n* **Target filtering**: Used frame differencing and background subtraction to remove stationary stars so only moving objects remain.\n* **Object verification**: Tested YOLO models to confirm the moving target was a satellite rather than planes, clouds, or camera sensor noise.\n* **Orbital math**: Used SGP4 orbit models and TLE satellite data to calculate the exact path and timing of each pass ahead of time.\n* **Motor steering**: Wrote control software in C++ and Python over RS-232 serial cables to drive the motorized mount and keep targets centered.\n* **Web dashboard**: Built a web interface in React and ASP.NET MVC to schedule passes, watch the live camera feed, and log tracking accuracy.\n\n---\n\n## Technologies Used\n\n* **Computer Vision & Image Processing**: OpenCV, Frame Differencing, Background Subtraction, Thresholding, Feature Detection, Pillow (PIL)\n* **Machine Learning**: PyTorch, YOLO (Object Detection), ML.NET\n* **Orbital Mechanics & Control Systems**: SGP4 Propagation, Two-Line Element (TLE) Datasets, Coordinate Transforms (RA/Dec to Az/El), RS-232 Serial Protocols, Closed-Loop PID Control\n* **Languages**: Python, C++, C, C#, TypeScript, JavaScript, SQL, Bash\n* **Web & Frameworks**: React, ASP.NET MVC, .NET Core, RESTful APIs, AJAX / Fetch, HTML5, CSS3\n* **Systems & Environment**: Embedded Linux, Multithreading, Asynchronous I/O, Git\n"
