    "raw": "---\ntitle: 'County Asset & Document Management Platform'\npublishedAt: '2024-05-15'\ndateRange: 'Jan 2024 - May 2024'\nsummary: 'Replaced an outdated desktop database with a centralized web application and RESTful backend, migrating legacy records with zero downtime.'\ntechStack: 'PHP, MySQL, MariaDB, JavaScript, Apache, Linux, RESTful APIs, HTML5, CSS3, PDO, RBAC, Bash, Cron, Git'\n---\n\n## The Problem\n\nCounty staff were tracking physical equipment, property, and official documents using a shared desktop Microsoft Access database.\n\nBecause Access was not built for multiple people to use at once, staff had frequent problems:\n\n* Files would lock up when two people opened them at the same time.\n* Searches and record lookups were slow.\n* The file was at risk of getting corrupted during edits.\n\nAs a Software Engineer on contract for Chippewa County Information Systems (Jan 2024 - May 2024), I was hired to replace the desktop file with a secure, centralized web application accessible from standard web browsers on the county network.\n\n---\n\n## What I Built\n\n* **Database migration**: Designed a clean relational schema in MySQL and MariaDB, wrote migration scripts in PHP and SQL, and migrated all historical records with zero data loss.\n* **Fast web interface**: Built a clean interface in vanilla JavaScript using Fetch and AJAX so staff could search, filter, and edit records instantly without full page reloads.\n* **Secure backend APIs**: Wrote modular PHP REST endpoints using PDO prepared statements to handle lookups, edits, and file uploads securely.\n* **Custom admin dashboard**: Built dedicated in-app admin pages for adding users, managing roles, and setting department permissions without exposing raw database tools.\n* **Audit log viewer**: Added an audit history page with timestamps and user names so administrators can see who modified any record.\n* **Export tools**: Built one-click report tools so staff can export filtered data to CSV, JSON, or formatted PDF files for county audits.\n* **Server setup**: Deployed the app on a dedicated Linux virtual machine with automated daily backup cron jobs and strict file permissions.\n\n---\n\n## Technologies Used\n\n* **Backend & APIs**: PHP, RESTful APIs, PDO (Prepared Statements), Apache 2.4, mod_rewrite, Session Management\n* **Database Architecture**: MySQL, MariaDB, 3NF Normalization, B-Tree Indexing, Composite Indexing, Foreign Keys, ACID Transactions\n* **Frontend Development**: Vanilla JavaScript (ES6+ Fetch / AJAX), HTML5, CSS3, Responsive UI\n* **Security & Administration**: Role-Based Access Control (RBAC), Custom Admin Dashboards, User Management, Bcrypt Password Hashing, Audit Logging\n* **Infrastructure & Tooling**: Linux Virtual Machine, Bash Automation, Cron Scheduling, Automated Backups, Git\n"
